# Git push policy

**Source of truth:** `local-commits-push-main.mdc`.

- Commit locally on **main** after each meaningful change.
- **Never** `git push origin main` unless the user clearly asks (“push to main”, “push all to main”, “merge to main”).
- Then push **once**: a single `git push origin main` of every local commit.
- “Push” without naming main → do **not** push `origin/main`.
- Never force-push `main`.
